  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Ranger Energy’s niche in high‑spec well servicing and production‑focused work benefits from robust demand as operators shift spending toward maintaining existing wells. The ECHO hybrid rig program and integration of the AWS acquisition strengthen its competitive position versus frac‑heavy peers and support margin stability. First‑quarter working‑capital pressures and negative free cash flow created a temporary drag, but utilization and operational momentum are expected to improve through the second half of 2026.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is executing a deliberate pivot toward less‑cyclical production services, concentrating on high‑spec rigs and hybrid technology to differentiate. Piper Sandler raised its price target and maintained an Overweight rating, signaling confidence in this direction. Despite near‑term cash‑flow headwinds, the company’s strategic acquisitions and focused operational execution are building credibility for a margin recovery later in the year.",
